WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.990
Hold a flame to sugar, and it burns.

2
00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:07.030
All its energy escapes at
once, as heat and light.

3
00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:10.670
Your cells break down the same
sugar, with the same oxygen,

4
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:13.640
into the same carbon dioxide and water.

5
00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:17.390
They release the same total
energy, in every living cell,

6
00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:22.470
day and night: plants,
fungi, bacteria, and you.

7
00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:26.960
So how do your cells release that
energy slowly enough to use it?

8
00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:29.930
In this mission, you'll
see where the energy goes:

9
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.610
into a molecule called ATP,
which powers the cell's work.

10
00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:37.090
Then you'll follow
glucose into glycolysis,

11
00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:41.880
the first stage of respiration,
as it splits into pyruvate.

12
00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:47.230
Your mission: find out how cells release
sugar's energy slowly enough to use.
